sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-16> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Animals with robust morphogenetic control due to high plasticity are resistant to perturbation at many scales: they regenerate lost limbs and organs, readily suppress cancer, and resist aging, contrary to the expectation that easy access to undifferentiated cells should make them highly cancer-prone.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Animals with robust regeneration also resist cancer and aging";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “Beginner’s mind: self-organization on the fly as the origin of multiscale competency”. Scope: Animals across taxa, especially highly regenerative ones such as planaria and salamanders"
}
